    "agent_messages": [
      "I'll start by reading the existing code to understand the structure and conventions, then implement the bulk-reject Action as specified.\nLet me explore the internal directory structure:\nNow let me examine the existing protocol and candidate packages:\nLet me read the existing code files:\nNow let me check the app package to understand the Identity structure:\nNow let me check the cmd directory to understand the entry point:\nNow let me check the go.mod to understand dependencies:\nNow I have a complete understanding of the codebase. Let me implement the bulk-reject action. Based on my analysis:\n\n1. I need to create a new Transition for \"bulk-reject.v4\" in the action package (but it's protected, so I'll declare it in `internal/candidate`)\n2. I need to add the bulk-reject handler to `internal/candidate/approval.go`\n3. I need to register the new route in `protocol.Routes` in the HTTP adapter\n\nLet me implement this:\nNow let me verify the code compiles:\nExcellent! Let me run the tests to make sure everything works:\nPerfect! Let me verify the implementation is complete by reviewing the changes:\nPerfect! The implementation is complete. Let me verify it one more time by building and running a quick check:\nExcellent! The implementation is complete and verified. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added the bulk-reject Action (`POST /purchases/bulk-reject`) to the existing service. The implementation follows all specifications and conventions:\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**File: `internal/candidate/approval.go`**\n- Added a new `Reject` transition variable with:\n  - `Operation: \"bulk-reject.v4\"` (matches schema constraints)\n  - `From: \"submitted\"` and `To: \"rejected\"` (status transitions)\n  - `Field: \"rejectedIds\"` (response field name)\n- Created a `reject` handler function that:\n  - Calls `executor.Run()` with the new Reject transition\n  - Adapts `action.Rejection` errors to `protocol.Rejection` (as required)\n  - Returns results with proper idempotency headers and HTTP status codes\n- Registered the new path `\"/purchases/bulk-reject\"` in `protocol.Routes`\n\n### How It Works\n\n1. **Shared HTTP Adapter**: The `protocol.HTTP` adapter handles all validation, identity binding, and request/response formatting for both endpoints\n2. **Action Kernel**: The `action.Executor.Run()` method manages:\n   - Transaction safety\n   - Eligibility checking via RLS (approver can only reject others' submitted purchases)\n   - Idempotency using `Idempotency-Key` header\n   - Audit trail in `ApprovalAudit` table\n   - Action metadata in `ActionRequest` table\n3. **Concurrency**: The same kernel handles concurrent batch operations with proper conflict detection (409 for hash mismatches, 4xx for eligibility failures)\n\n### Preserved Behavior\n\n- The existing `bulk-approve` endpoint operates unchanged\n- All shared validations (request body format, identity, header limits) apply equally\n- The existing `action.Approve` transition remains untouched\n- The schema already supports both operations via v4 constraints\n\nThe implementation is production-ready and follows all specified requirements for idempotency, concurrency control, audit trails, and error handling."
